at the fish market in france's biggest  fishing port they're nervous  some here say they've already lost  nearly 50 percent of their income after  their boats weren't granted a license to  fish in british waters  what we don't understand is why some  boats were given licenses and others  weren't some of these boats have been  fishing in these waters for generations  the ocean became the latest battleground  between the uk and the european union  under a post-brexit trade deal which  came into force this year  it meant both sides could control who  could fish in their waters  france accuses the uk of unfairly  denying permission to dozens of its  vessels  fishermen and boulongsomer rely on  british waters for their catch but the  relationship goes both ways because for  the british fishing industry france is  the gateway to europe and they depend on  ports like this for access to the  continent  if the uk doesn't resolve the issue  france is threatening to roll out a  series of sanctions including tougher  checks on trucks going to and from the  uk  and preventing british fishing boats  from docking and unloading their catch  the uk says it's considering legal  action if the measures go ahead  the announcement of brexit we knew  there'd be a lot of problems for the  fishing industry what's happening now is  not a surprise and the biggest losers  will be the british fishermen and the  french fishermen  and not just them  there's concern here that thousands of  jobs could be affected including those  who process the fish that's brought  ashore from british boats  what we want is for everyone to be able  to work for everyone to be able to go  anywhere respecting each other's jobs  for us all to have equal rights and work  hand in hand like before  this city is home to a statue that pays  tribute to the close relations between  the uk and france but that  relationship's being sorely tested  and as politicians argue over their  futures some in the fishing community  feel they're being left out at sea  alexia o'brien al jazeera bologna sumer  northern france
 

